<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Livonian Brothers of the Sword</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1202–<a href="/years/1237">1237</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Sword Brothers, Order of the Sword Brothers</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Livonian Brothers of the Sword were a military order founded in 1202 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-of-riga">Albert of Riga</a> to conquer pagan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a>. Over two decades they subdued the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonians">Livs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latgalians">Latgalians</a> and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonians">Estonians</a>. After a heavy defeat by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuanians">Lithuanians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/semigallians">Semigallians</a> at Saule in 1236, the survivors were absorbed into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> in 1237 as its Livonian branch.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/livonian-brothers-of-the-sword.jpg" alt="Livonian Brothers of the Sword" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LivoniaKnight.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
